    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "*** FIRST OFFER OF €420,000 SECURES ***\r\n\r\nBARRY AUCTIONEERS & VALUERS are delighted to bring to the market this historic 7-bedroom, 2,508 sq. ft house in Monkstown. This family home offers a rare opportunity to restore and modernize a grand property with stunning potential. Built in 1850, the home retains its period character, with high ceilings, large windows, and traditional architectural features, while requiring updates to bring it into the 21st century. The generous living spaces are filled with light, providing captivating views over the water, creating a serene and picturesque backdrop.\r\n\r\nThe seven spacious bedrooms are perfect for reimagining into contemporary retreats, while the expansive reception areas can be transformed into stylish entertaining spaces. The property boasts beautiful original details, such as large bay windows  and fireplaces, which can be preserved or enhanced as part of the modernisation.\r\n\r\nSet on just less shy of half an acre with picturesque gardens and offering direct views of the water, this home is ideal for those seeking to infuse their own style into a piece of Monkstown’s history. With the right vision and investment, this property can become a stunning family home in one of Cork’s most sought-after coastal locations.\r\n\r\nMonkstown is a charming village located just outside Cork city in Ireland, situated along the southern coast about 10 kilometres from the city centre, and is known for its picturesque surroundings, combining natural beauty with a peaceful village atmosphere. The area is notable for its proximity to Cork Harbour, one of the largest natural harbours in the world, which offers stunning views and opportunities for outdoor activities like walking, sailing, and birdwatching.\r\nMonkstown is home to a mix of traditional and modern houses, and its quaint streets feature local cafés and pubs, contributing to its welcoming, community-focused vibe. The village is also known for its tennis club, sailing club and Monkstown golf club  a popular course with scenic views over the harbour. With its easy access to Cork city, it provides a quieter, more suburban setting while still being close to urban amenities. It’s a great spot for those who enjoy coastal life and the outdoors while remaining connected to the city.\r\n\r\nHistory of the house:\r\nThis property was once the home of the late Denny Lane, a Cork poet, businessman and Young Irelander, who composed the famous song ‘Carrigdhoun’. There is a Mass Rock not very far from the house, close to the ‘Cut and Cover’ where mass was offered during the Penal Days. At the back of the house is a spring well, where many of the villagers used to get their water when the local supply failed. The grounds of this house ran uphill behind the church and Denny Lane had his own pathway to the church, known as ‘The Priest’s Steps’. The house probably gave its name to the hill which is still known as Fairy Hill. The original name of the hill was Darling Hill. Henry Warren occupied the house during the 1840s and Dr. Henry O’Brien lived there during the 1850’s.The present owners have resided here since 1962.  \r\n\r\nViewing is a must to fully appreciate."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hallway:\r\nCarpet flooring, feature staircase.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 8.5m x 5.5m\r\nCarpet flooring, large bay window overlooking the water, and feature fireplace.\r\n\r\nDining Room: 4.5m x 4.0m \r\nCarpet flooring, feature tiled fireplace, two windows overlooking rear garden. \r\n\r\nL shaped Kitchen: 6.3m x 4.2 \r\nFully fitted kitchen with kerosene AGA, stainless steel sink & drainer. Spiral stairs to back landing.\r\n\r\nGuest WC: \r\nWC & WHB\r\n\r\nSunroom:  5.7m x 4.2m \r\nCarpet flooring, marble fireplace, large patio doors to front garden.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: 5m x 4.3m  \r\nCarpet, large bay window with water views.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:  3.5m x 2.6m \r\nCarpet flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3:  3.2m x 3.2m \r\nCarpet flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4:  3.2m x 3.0m \r\nCarpet flooring.\r\n\r\nBathroom: 3m x 2.7m  \r\nLino floor, tiled walls, 4-piece bathroom suite.\r\n\r\nSecond Floor:\r\n\r\nBedroom 5:  5.4m x 3.5m \r\nCarpet flooring, large bay window overlooking the water.\r\n\r\nBedroom 6:  4.4m x 3.5m \r\nCarpet flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 7:  4.2m x 2.7m \r\nCarpet flooring.\r\n\r\nBathroom:  2.7m x 2.2m \r\nLino flooring, 3-piece bathroom suite .\r\n\r\nOutside: \r\nLawned gardens to the front with pedestrian access. Parking to the rear and also derelict coach house at the rear which has incredible potential."
      },
